{"game": "the-first-descendant", "language": "english", "appid": 2074920, "month": "2026-06", "window": 4, "start_date": 1782172800, "end_date": 1782863999, "month_true_total": 149, "quota": 5, "returned": 5, "pulled_at": "2026-10-01 15:49:39 UTC", "reviews": [{"recommendationid": "229267499", "author": {"steamid": "76561199216361771", "personaname": "Nef", "persona_status": "in-game", "profile_url": "https://steamcommunity.com/profiles/76561199216361771/", "num_games_owned": 21, "num_reviews": 16, "playtime_forever": 8498, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 2272, "playtime_at_review": 4918, "last_played": 1790869766, "avatar": "50767cea96889a121066ed45c098873cb258f8f3"}, "language": "english", "review": "My Review – The First Descendant\n\n1. I've spent over 500 hours in Warframe and reached the endgame, so this is based on my own experience.\n2. Compared to Warframe, The First Descendant respects my time more. An hour of grinding feels much more rewarding, and I make noticeable progress every session.\n3. The developers are surprisingly generous. I returned after leaving the game in 2024, and by completing a few quests and missions, I received a lot of valuable endgame materials through the mailbox. It made coming back feel worth it.\n4. In Warframe, if you return after a long break, your account is basically where you left it. That's fine, but it doesn't feel nearly as welcoming for returning players.\n5. Right now, I'm having a great time with The First Descendant. The progression feels satisfying, and personally, I enjoy it a bit more than Warframe at the moment.\n\nIf you're curious about the game, I'd definitely recommend giving it a try.", "timestamp_created": 1782846815, "timestamp_updated": 1782846855, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 4, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.487945437431335449", "comment_count": 3, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_rel